    "id": "p23-challenge-q2-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "2",
    "prompt": "Show that $\\sin420^{\\circ}\\cos405^{\\circ}+\\cos420^{\\circ}\\sin405^{\\circ}=\\dfrac{\\sqrt3+1}{2\\sqrt2}$.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$\\dfrac{\\sqrt3+1}{2\\sqrt2}$.\n\nSubtract $360^{\\circ}$ from each angle, then substitute the exact ratios for $60^{\\circ}$ and $45^{\\circ}$.",
      "worked": "Since $420^{\\circ}-360^{\\circ}=60^{\\circ}$ and $405^{\\circ}-360^{\\circ}=45^{\\circ}$,\n\n$$\\begin{align*}\\sin420^{\\circ}\\cos405^{\\circ}+\\cos420^{\\circ}\\sin405^{\\circ}&=\\sin60^{\\circ}\\cos45^{\\circ}+\\cos60^{\\circ}\\sin45^{\\circ}\\\\\\sin420^{\\circ}\\cos405^{\\circ}+\\cos420^{\\circ}\\sin405^{\\circ}&=\\frac{\\sqrt3}{2}\\cdot\\frac1{\\sqrt2}+\\frac12\\cdot\\frac1{\\sqrt2}\\\\\\sin420^{\\circ}\\cos405^{\\circ}+\\cos420^{\\circ}\\sin405^{\\circ}&=\\frac{\\sqrt3}{2\\sqrt2}+\\frac1{2\\sqrt2}\\\\\\sin420^{\\circ}\\cos405^{\\circ}+\\cos420^{\\circ}\\sin405^{\\circ}&=\\frac{\\sqrt3+1}{2\\sqrt2}.\\end{align*}$$",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 52
  },
